-- title:
--   Descent of integrality from ℚ̄[j,j_N] to (A∩ K)[j]
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $N$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid N$; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism into a field $k$ of characteristic $q$. Write $A_0 := A \cap K$ for the intersection, inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of the subring underlying $A$ with the subring underlying $K$. Let $y$ be a Laurent series with coefficients in $A_0$, and let $g_0$ be an element of the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the elements of the field $\mathbb{Q}(\mathrm{divisorExpansions}\,N)$, and assume that the Laurent series underlying $g_0$ is the coefficientwise image of $y$ along $A_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume further that $g_0$ is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra of that field generated by the two elements obtained by pushing the $\mathsf{q}$-expansion $\mathsf{q}^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$ of $j$, and its image under the substitution $\mathsf{q} \mapsto \mathsf{q}^{N}$, from $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$. Then the Laurent series $g_0$ is integral over the subring of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the constant series attached to the elements of $A_0$ together with $\mathsf{q}^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNum}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the descent of integrality of a modular function of level $N$ from the geometric coefficient ring $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[j, j_N]$ to the arithmetic ring $(A\cap K)[j]$, available at a residue characteristic $q$ prime to the level, the hypothesis on $g_0$ being that its $\mathsf{q}$-expansion already has coefficients in $A \cap K$. It is used in the analysis of prolongations of places in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_mem_jIntegralClosure_ord_residues_pos_and_eq_zero_of_ne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_mem_jIntegralClosure_ord_residues_pos_and_eq_zero_of_ne).
